<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_14_1" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_14_1" name="14.1 Administer the workforce" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>Three of the four processes are drawn. 14.1.2 the organisational structure is SPEC - it is held continuously and read by everything that approves, costs or assigns, and has no instance boundary of its own.

ONE EVENT DRIVES THE WHOLE GROUP: a person joins, moves, changes status or leaves. Everything else in the flow is a consequence, which is why access provisioning at 14.1.4 hangs off the worker record rather than off a request. Access granted on request bypasses the qualification restriction 14.2.4 exists to apply, and the field application then offers work the person may not do.

14.1.3 OWNS THE PERSON STATUS RECORD and 3.5.4 is the scheduling view of it. The flow only ever publishes status outward; there is no path by which a status set in scheduling comes back in. Setting availability in two places is how a restricted person gets dispatched, and this is the group where that would happen.

49 CFR Part 199 is the one hard regulatory input and it is gas only. A positive result or a refusal removes a covered employee from availability - a workforce fact, not a scheduling one. Electric utilities are not covered by Part 199 at all.

A leaver's record is retired, not deleted. The work they performed stays attributable and their qualification evidence has to outlive the employment that produced it, because 192.805 evidence is read long afterwards.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_14_1_lanes">
      <lane id="l_141_hr" name="Workforce administration">
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_what</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_new</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_mov</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_stat</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_p199</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_leave</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_pub</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_141_it" name="Access and devices">
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_acc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_prov</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_give</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_141_take</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_141_start" name="A person joins, moves, changes status or leaves"><messageEventDefinition id="n_141_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_141_what" name="Which event"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_141_new" name="Create the worker record and its identifier"><documentation>14.1.1. The identifier every completed work record will point at. Reusing one silently reattributes history.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_141_mov" name="Change role, craft or base location"><documentation>14.1.1.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_141_stat" name="Set availability status with its reason and period"><documentation>14.1.3. The reason travels with the status: a qualification lapse, a medical restriction and annual leave are three different facts.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <businessRuleTask id="n_141_p199" name="Apply the Part 199 outcome"><documentation>14.1.3. Gas covered employees only. A positive result or a refusal removes the person from availability. Electric utilities are not covered.</documentation></businessRuleTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_141_leave" name="Retire the record, keeping the work history"><documentation>14.1.1. Retired, not deleted. Qualification evidence outlives the employment.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_141_acc" name="Derive access from role and qualification"><documentation>14.1.4. Derived, never requested. Access granted directly bypasses 14.2.4.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_141_prov" name="Provision or remove"/>
    <sendTask id="n_141_give" name="Provision accounts, device and field application"><documentation>14.1.4.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_141_take" name="Remove access and evidence the removal"><documentation>14.1.4. Evidenced, not assumed. An account outliving employment is a workforce failure before it is an IT one.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_141_pub" name="Publish the worker, status and structure outward"><documentation>14.1.1, 14.1.3. PUBLISH only. 3.5.4 is the scheduling view of this record and never writes back to it.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_141_end" name="Workforce record current and published"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_start_n_141_what" sourceRef="n_141_start" targetRef="n_141_what" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_what_n_141_new" sourceRef="n_141_what" targetRef="n_141_new" name="joiner"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_what_n_141_mov" sourceRef="n_141_what" targetRef="n_141_mov" name="role or location change"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_what_n_141_stat" sourceRef="n_141_what" targetRef="n_141_stat" name="availability change"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_what_n_141_leave" sourceRef="n_141_what" targetRef="n_141_leave" name="leaver"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_stat_n_141_p199" sourceRef="n_141_stat" targetRef="n_141_p199" name="gas covered employee"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[regime = "part199"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_p199_n_141_acc" sourceRef="n_141_p199" targetRef="n_141_acc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_stat_n_141_acc" sourceRef="n_141_stat" targetRef="n_141_acc" name="other reason"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_new_n_141_acc" sourceRef="n_141_new" targetRef="n_141_acc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_mov_n_141_acc" sourceRef="n_141_mov" targetRef="n_141_acc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_leave_n_141_acc" sourceRef="n_141_leave" targetRef="n_141_acc" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_acc_n_141_prov" sourceRef="n_141_acc" targetRef="n_141_prov" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_prov_n_141_give" sourceRef="n_141_prov" targetRef="n_141_give" name="entitled"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_prov_n_141_take" sourceRef="n_141_prov" targetRef="n_141_take" name="no longer entitled"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[entitled = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_give_n_141_pub" sourceRef="n_141_give" targetRef="n_141_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_take_n_141_pub" sourceRef="n_141_take" targetRef="n_141_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_141_pub_n_141_end" sourceRef="n_141_pub" targetRef="n_141_end" name=""/>
  </process>
